Map whole-file reads on Linux via Data.ReadingOptions.mappedIfLocal

Swift 6's Linux Foundation never maps for .mappedIfSafe, so every whole-file
Data(contentsOf:options:) is a malloc plus a full read where Darwin gets a
lazy mmap. models import opens the safetensors twice before printing
Detected, and the server's two SHA-256 paths and GRPCFileUploader each malloc
whole checkpoints. mappedIfLocal is .mappedIfSafe on Darwin and .alwaysMapped
on Linux, which FoundationEssentials honours with a real mmap. Darwin
behaviour is byte-identical.
